      "text": "plates preserved that Lamanites might be saved, D&C 3:20. those who believe, repent, are baptized, and endure shall be saved, D&C 18:22 (20:25, 29; 53:7; 68:9; 112:29). Jesus Christ only name whereby man can be saved, D&C 18:23 (20:29). those who keep not commandments cannot be saved, D&C 18:46 (42:60). man cannot be saved without faith, D&C 33:12. Israel to be saved, D&C 35:25. elders to cry, Save yourselves from this generation, D&C 36:6. go out from among wicked, save yourselves, D&C 38:42. he who does commandments will be saved, D&C 42:60 (100:17). Saints to save all money that they can, to purchase lands, D&C 48:4. he who receives the Son will be saved, D&C 49:5. he only is saved who endures to end, D&C 53:7. he who believes and is baptized shall be saved, D&C 68:9 (112:29). through Jesus all may be saved whom the Father puts into his power, D&C 76:42. Christ saves all except sons of perdition, D&C 76:43. angels sent forth from God to save life, D&C 77:8. all who call on the Lord and keep his commandments shall be saved, D&C 100:17. impossible for man to be saved in ignorance, D&C 131:6. they who are not married by new and everlasting covenant remain without exaltation in their saved condition, D&C 132:17. enter ye into my law and ye shall be saved, D&C 132:32. children who die before age of accountability are saved in celestial kingdom, D&C 137:10. mankind may be saved through Atonement and by obedience, D&C 138:4.",
